  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing recorded $99.8M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The market reached 427 awards with an average award size of $234K. Obligations fell 91.0% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows $1.1B in FY22, $1.5B in FY23, $2B in FY24, $1.6B in FY25, and $1.1B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer in FY2027 to date with $99.1M in obligations. The Department of Justice, Department of State, and Environmental Protection Agency follow with $667K, $52.1K, and $35.6K respectively. WELCH ALLYN, INC. leads vendors in FY2027 to date with $30.5M in obligations, followed by OLYMPUS AMERICA INC with $18.3M and SCRIPTPRO USA INC with $7.3M. The top ten vendors together illustrate a concentrated supplier list for the current fiscal-year to date total of $99.8M. Contracting activity so far reflects a much smaller fiscal-year total than recent peak years, with most FY2027 to date dollars concentrated at the Department of Veterans Affairs and a handful of large vendors.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations total $99.8M compared with $2B in FY24, $1.6B in FY25, $1.5B in FY23, $1.1B in FY26, and $1.1B in FY22. Obligations fell 91.0% year over year. The award count for FY2027 to date is 427 with an average award size of $234K. The current-year total is much smaller than recent full fiscal years and concentrated among a few buyers and vendors."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors drive FY2027 to date obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $99.1M in FY2027 to date, accounting for most of the NAICS 339112 total. The Department of Justice obligated $667K, the Department of State obligated $52.1K, and the Environmental Protection Agency obligated $35.6K. WELCH ALLYN, INC. obligated $30.5M and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC obligated $18.3M in FY2027 to date, with SCRIPTPRO USA INC at $7.3M and other vendors ranging from $2.3M to $6M."
      }
    ]
  },
